@startuml
title Activity Diagram: 2. Develop Branch Workflow (Staging Environment)

' This diagram conceptually starts after the "Feature Branch Workflow"
' where code is merged/integrated into Develop.

|Git/GitHub|
start
note left: Triggered by push/merge to Develop Branch
' Start of "Develop Branch Workflow" partition from original diagram
:Receives push/merge to Develop Branch;
:Triggers Jenkins (Develop Pipeline);

|Jenkins (CI/CD Pipeline)|
:Pipeline for Develop Branch starts;
:Checkout source code from Develop Branch;
note right: This code has passed unit & intra-service tests from feature branches.

fork
  group Frontend Image Build (Develop)
    :Build Frontend Docker image (Nginx + Vue.js);
    |Docker Registry|
    :Push Frontend Docker image (tagged for develop/staging);
  end group
fork again
  group Backend Image Build (Develop)
    :Build Backend Docker image(s);
    |Docker Registry|
    :Push Backend Docker image(s) (tagged for develop/staging);
  end group
end fork

|Jenkins (CI/CD Pipeline)|
:Deploy to Develop/Staging Kubernetes Environment;
|Kubernetes Cluster\n (Develop/Staging Environment)|
:Pulls new images;
:Deploys/Updates containers;
:Develop/Staging environment updated;

|Jenkins (CI/CD Pipeline)|
:Run Inter-Service Integration Tests & E2E Smoke Tests against Develop/Staging Environment;
if (Inter-service Integration tests pass on Develop/Staging?) then (yes)
  :Develop Branch is stable;
  :Notify designated Developer(s)/Team Lead: "Code on Develop ready for review and promotion to Main";
  |Developer|
  :Initiates code review process for merging Develop to Main;
  note right: Successful review & merge triggers the "Main Branch Workflow"
  '(Approval & merge to Main happens here after review - manual step)
else (no)
  |Jenkins (CI/CD Pipeline)|
  :Notify ALL Developers of Inter-Service Integration test failure on Develop/Staging;
  end
endif
' End of "Develop Branch Workflow" partition from original diagram

stop
@enduml